Architecture R-77 and the S8 fit rows, replacing the earlier fit request's uniqueItems-object figure: a uniqueItems array of objects passes up to about 6,500 objects of two string members (2.1%) but only about 1,700 of one number member (0.19%) at the 10 MiB default, at the work limit; the review's 6,600 / 2.3% held only for string members. Add the dense shapes, each the largest valid body measured:
- decimals under minimum and maximum: 53%, working-set limit;
- [timestamp, value] pairs under prefixItems: 63%, decoded limit;
- [lon, lat] pairs under minItems/maxItems 2 with bounded numbers: 38%, working-set limit;
- a {t, v} time series under required and additionalProperties false: 52%, reservation limit;
- uniqueItems integer ids: 33%, working-set limit;
- uniqueItems short string tags: 42%, working-set limit;
- composed orders: 56%.

confirmed.evidence:
I reproduced this on the current working tree with a scratch overlay at /tmp/claude-0/-home-user-ruralz/0aabfe6e-34a6-51d2-9b9b-23886b703760/scratchpad/v51/: zz_probe_test.go, zz_check_test.go, zz_helper_test.go and overlay.json. Command: `CGO_ENABLED=0 go test -count=1 -overlay <scratch>/v51/overlay.json -run 'TestZZMetaBypass|TestZZCheck' -v ./internal/filter/validation/jsonschema/`.

Results:
- {"multipleOf":0} on its own is refused with RZ-CFG-005, "exclusiveMinimum: got 0, want 0 at /multipleOf". Check also emits one RZ-CFG-005 at spec.config.schema.multipleOf.
- These schemas each give CompileSchema err=nil, Factory.Build ok and 0 Check diagnostics. Then both Schema.Validate and Filter.Handle(onRequestBody, application/json) panic with "division by zero":
  - {"$ref":"#/additionalItems","additionalItems":{"multipleOf":0}} with body 5
  - {"$ref":"#a","additionalItems":{"$anchor":"a","multipleOf":0}}
  - {"$dynamicRef":"#d","additionalItems":{"$dynamicAnchor":"d","multipleOf":0}}
  - {"$ref":"item.json","additionalItems":{"$id":"item.json","multipleOf":0}}
  - {"type":"object","properties":{"price":{"$ref":"#/additionalItems/properties/p"}},"additionalItems":{"properties":{"p":{"type":"number","multipleOf":0}}}} with body {"price":19.99}
- These compile with no diagnostic and accept every body (Validate returns "", true; Handle continues):
  - {"$ref":"#/additionalItems","additionalItems":{"type":"strng"}}
  - the same with "type":5, "enum":5, "required":5 or "properties":{"a":5}
- Control: {"$ref":"#/$defs/x","$defs":{"x":{"type":"strng"}}} is refused with RZ-CFG-005 at /$defs/x/type. So the only gap is the additionalItems position.

Why it happens:
- walk.go:282-296 and :312-314 apply only the walker's own rules (patterns, numbers, name lists) to live positions under additionalItems. They do not apply the meta-schema.
- metacheck.go:49-51 marks the whole keyword tree as checked, so these positions never enter checkOrder.
- In the library (santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema v6.0.3), roots.go:70-77 marks every collected position, additionalItems included (draft.go:45), as processed. ensureSubschema (roots.go:197-200) then returns before rr.validate. validator.go:547 runs new(big.Rat).Quo(num, 0).
- Check (check.go:27-36) shares compileRaw, so the offline check misses it too.
- The executor recovers Filter panics (internal/gateway/executor/executor.go:262-317), so Handle becomes undecided: RZ-RT-011 when failureMode is closed, or a skip when it is open. Schema.Validate panics directly.

Spec: this breaks 07 req 75, "Offline checks, RZ-CFG-005 ... compile with santhosh-tekuri/jsonschema/v6 using default draft 2020-12", applied identically in all three binaries. A schema the draft 2020-12 meta-schema refuses, once it is compiled, passes CompileSchema, Check and Build. No documented deviation covers it. w3-s2b-result.json does not mention additionalItems. w3-s2-wp51-fix-result.json mentions it only for the legacy items/additionalItems branches below draft 2020-12. doc.go:60-63 says the walker's rules "apply there only then", but says nothing about the meta-schema check being skipped.

